# Docker build context (repository root). The Dockerfile copies the whole context (COPY . .) into
# the build stage, so anything not listed here goes into the build, and src/ and prisma/ go on
# into the image. Keep secrets, local state, docs and tooling out. The build needs only
# package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, .npmrc, the sources and their config (src, prisma, public,
# *.config.ts, tsconfig.json) and deploy/staging/entrypoint.sh and collect-node-modules.mjs.

# Settings and secrets: never in the image (every setting comes from the environment at run
# time). This also leaves out the committed template .env.example, which the image does not need.
**/.env*
deploy/staging/.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.crt
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.netrc
**/*credentials*.json
**/*.secret
.gitleaksignore

# Local state, build output and dependencies (the build installs its own)
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.git
**/.next
out
src/generated
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.vercel
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Tests' results, and the end-to-end tests: they are not part of the image. playwright.config.ts
# imports them, so it goes too (otherwise the type check in `next build` fails).
coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
e2e
playwright.config.ts

# Docs and agent tooling
docs
_bmad
_bmad-output
api-docs
apolles
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.superpowers
.claude
.agents
.gemini
.opencode
.github
